WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.030
It wasn't until late in the first season of
NCIS: New Orleans that viewers met ATF agent

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:10.240
Sonja Percy, played by Tony-nominated actress
Shalita Grant.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.879
Once she became a regular on the show in season
two, she quickly became a favorite thanks

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:20.240
to her penchant for calling out BS and her
great chemistry with Agent Christopher LaSalle,

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.830
played by Lucas Black.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:26.620
As anybody who watches network crime procedurals
will tell you, all good things must come to

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.380
an end, and no NCIS agent is forever.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:34.610
After three seasons on the show, Grant decided
to hand in her badge, and the character of

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.500
Agent Percy was retired.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.730
Any time an actor leaves a hit show, it always
raises the question: was their ouster a natural

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.390
progression of the story, or was something
going on behind the scenes?

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.290
"Coming in with some attitude.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.840
Let me lighten that load for you."

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.890
"Hate to spoil the party, but we gotta talk."

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:57.370
Throughout the fourth season of the show,
it was clear to the NCIS: New Orleans team

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.940
that something was eating at Agent Percy.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.720
She seemed restless and distracted, and made
a few bad calls that were out of character.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.490
In her penultimate episode on the show, "Welcome
to the Jungle," Percy revealed that she interviewed

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.620
for a position with the FBI.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:16.260
Her issues, it seems, were caused by a nagging
feeling that she needed to move on to something

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:16.960
new.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.750
Although she was offered the FBI job, Percy
initially declined it, as she didn't want

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.100
to upset her NCIS squadmates.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.690
In Percy's final episode, "High Stakes," she
and Agent LaSalle were assigned to work a

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:31.090
sting operation at a poker game.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:36.280
Percy ended up in an SUV with the perp they
were tracking and, in a split-second decision,

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.580
she rolled the vehicle to prevent him from
getting the upper hand on her.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:44.440
It was a very risky move that ended up paying
off, but it was further proof that Percy's

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:47.980
instincts were being affected by her feeling
of restlessness.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:53.670
In the end, Percy realized that the only reason
she turned down the FBI job was to avoid disappointing

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:57.220
other people, which wasn't the correct decision
to make for herself.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.420
At the end of the episode, she announced her
departure from the team.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:05.100
When Variety originally reported on Grant's
decision to leave, they cited sources who

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.100
said:

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:10.039
"The departure is amicable, and mutually agreed
upon between the actress and the producers."

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:14.569
In a later report on Deadline, the actress
herself claimed she was ready to move on.

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:19.340
The year after exiting the show, Grant landed
a recurring role on the final season of Santa

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.469
Clarita Diet.

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:22.540
"Good afternoon everyone.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.700
I'm Special Agent Tess Rogers with the FBI."

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:32.239
In 2017, while Grant was still on NCIS: New
Orleans, she did open up about the difficulties

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:36.019
of transitioning from theater to the world
of primetime crime dramas.

00:02:36.019 --> 00:02:38.260
In an interview with Lenny Letter, Grant said:

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.930
"I didn't realize just how different a procedural
is [...] I do come from theater, and I am

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:46.329
always looking for ways to be human and be
alive and in the moment.

00:02:46.329 --> 00:02:48.950
It is challenging to do that with a procedural."

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.440
She's far from the first actor to speak up
about the grind of filming twenty-two episode

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.120
seasons.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.159
Although she didn't cite those particular
issues when speaking about her exit, it seems

00:02:58.159 --> 00:03:02.519
likely that they played a role in her decision
to move on to different projects.

00:03:02.519 --> 00:03:07.069
One of those different projects may also shine
some light on what factors motivated her to

00:03:07.069 --> 00:03:08.069
leave the show.

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:13.019
It wasn't just her role on Santa Clarita Diet
that kept Grant busy after she left NCIS:

00:03:13.019 --> 00:03:14.019
New Orleans.

00:03:14.019 --> 00:03:18.439
The enterprising actress launched a hair care
line specifically for black women with Type

00:03:18.439 --> 00:03:20.569
4 hair called Four Naturals.

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:24.680
On the company's website, Grant opened up
about what inspired her to launch her haircare

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:25.320
line.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.240
She said:

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.749
"I found myself utterly wrecked after three
years on a television show that decimated

00:03:30.749 --> 00:03:36.279
my natural hair and my self-image [...] My
tight Type 4 hair was not welcome; instead,

00:03:36.279 --> 00:03:40.949
the producers and hair department had no issue
with my natural hair suffering or falling

00:03:40.949 --> 00:03:45.480
out to comply with the mandate to wear a ponytail
with little to no curl.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:49.370
After quitting what was once a dream job,
I told myself that I would turn that pain

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.469
into a platform."

00:03:50.469 --> 00:03:55.790
Although she didn't specify which show caused
the damage, NCIS: New Orleans is the actress'

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.269
only three-year-long stint on any series.

00:03:58.269 --> 00:04:02.750
It seems likely that it's the culprit, and
it seems this difficult environment could

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.219
be another reason Grant decided to leave.

00:04:05.219 --> 00:04:06.879
"I'm gonna miss you city mouse."

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.360
"I'll miss you too country mouse."

